  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 250 PM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nNear daily thunderstorm chances will remain through the weekend. \nUpper ridging will gradually back towards the west through the \nweekend and into next week with the weekend having the best \npotential of wetting rains. Guidance is currently suggesting a \n40 - 60 percent chance of a quarter of an inch or more over \nsouthwest into south central Nebraska Saturday and Sunday \nevening. Whereas early next week guidance suggests a 30 - 50 \npercent chance of a tenth of an inch falling across the same \narea. This is still subject to change as models become more \nrefined but remains enough of a signal now to highlight it. \n\nWeekend temperatures will remain below normal due to the easterly \nlow level flow and near overcast skies that will persist. Highs are \nexpected to only peak in the low 80s across areas along and south of \nI-80, with mid to upper 70s highs expected northward. Highs will \nwarm slightly to the low to mid 80s by next week but this will still \nremain about 5 degrees below normal.",
